# The sealed fixture is supplied by the kit at run time and is not ours to publish.
# Reason: the graded run mounts it read-only at MAKEFUN_INPUT_DIR; committing it would
# ship 248 KB of third-party snapshot data into a public repository for no gain.
input/snapshot.json

# The transcript bundle is a raw private session record, not a build artefact.
# Reason: the verify stage (docs/verify-stage-work_647d5c582d.md) found it contains a
# verbatim household conversation; publishing it to a public bounty repository is an
# irreversible disclosure no instruction in this item authorises. It is supplied to the
# grader from outside the tree via `check --transcripts transcripts.tar.gz`, which is
# exactly how pass 4 measured 11 passed / 2 failed. Father's word is required before it
# is ever committed. (declared-work discipline, work_fb464e49b9)
transcripts.tar.gz

# The handed-over session is extracted from the bundle for regeneration only; it is
# not a source file of the entry. WHY: bundle --session needs it on disk, and a
# tracked copy would make repo.dirty true on every rebuild (work_647d5c582d-s1).
sessions/
